{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">2021 AMC 10A #3</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2021 AMC 12A #3</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Arithmetic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Arithmetic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Vertical_Addition_and_Logic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Vertical Addition and Logic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Logic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Logic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of two natural numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66ca64ef6f493f784743300ed5b9af4c1f846cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17{,}402$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />. One of the two numbers is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. If the units digit of that number is erased, the other number is obtained. What is the difference of these two numbers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8365d0bc3bd8753032e496a082126ea91b672415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~10{,}272\\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~11{,}700\\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~13{,}362\\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~14{,}238\\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~15{,}426$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"555\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Algebra)\">Solution 1 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The units digit of a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> will always be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We add a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> whenever we multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. So, removing the units digit is equal to dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let the  smaller number (the one we get after removing the units digit) be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. This means the bigger number would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38666b2fe62287cf8268eceddbbc8aa47ccff05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>We know the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532e412562d63d4a4c537862c65c3ef182fff0ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a+a = 11a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/7/30788acaf36693d82f042e91daa4dea103871234.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11a=17402$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/931d1b3fb37d5176d5a833156038f23d1d60a4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1582$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />. The difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/4/d24add41af5583e9df3d03443815be29df841156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a-a = 9a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"102\" height=\"13\" />. So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbdc8f21cd2ed61b0bf21b5a8b596f959538f37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9(1582) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} ~14{,}238}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"182\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~abhinavg0627\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Arithmetic)\">Solution 2 (Arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the unit's place of a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the other integer must end with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, for both integers sum up to a number ending in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the unit's place of the difference must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/5/115e11f472361e53f627a66417f96cdfed51a037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />, and the only answer choice that ends with an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c033add6d8fd001f77c0c1b4531380a3ba620d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} ~14{,}238}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Another quick solution is to realize that the sum represents a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> added to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/7/af7a5bcbe3ff46fc5fad9d5f34a1dd027e3cf487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. The difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aede914ef25a6039761d27c1c435a6601807ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/2370b83ca83b66b729875f9b97f036cbeb18712c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> of the given sum.\n</p><p>~CoolJupiter 2021\n</p><p>~Extremelysupercooldude (Minor grammar edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Vertical_Addition_and_Logic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Vertical_Addition_and_Logic)\">Solution 3 (Vertical Addition and Logic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Vertical Addition and Logic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the larger number be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0f62356cfcce333c78602ef846a876e219f5af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{AB{,}CD0}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" /> It follows that the smaller number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfc39e1b3e9a47f81f665f5d69730039130b5c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{A{,}BCD}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" /> Adding vertically, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c44e347909afefc451d896500c564ad59cb01771.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{cccccc}   &amp; A &amp; B &amp; C &amp; D &amp; 0 \\\\ +\\quad &amp;   &amp; A &amp; B &amp; C &amp; D \\\\ \\hline   &amp;   &amp;   &amp;   &amp;   &amp;   \\\\ [-2.5ex]   &amp; 1 &amp; 7 &amp; 4 &amp; 0 &amp; 2 \\\\ \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"55\" />\nWorking from right to left, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61dd6a92108f96ce8b9940a52e71cc0d5c86228.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D=2\\implies C=8 \\implies B=5 \\implies A=1.\\]\" width=\"343\" height=\"13\" />\nThe larger number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a411735864570d5e0939baeb14d018e6027e04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15{,}820$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and the smaller number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fb5f03152c7ad7ea58c2fe2b1cb1e80ffa1f1ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1{,}582.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" /> Their difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9adb4ba9f5936651b1d308d663e4e8455c4f469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15{,}820-1{,}582=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} ~14{,}238}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"242\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Logic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Logic)\">Solution 4 (Logic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Logic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that the larger number has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> since it is divisible by 10. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the ten's digit of the larger number, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the units digit of the smaller number. Since the sum of the natural numbers has a unit's digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5fa11a4ce3ea4f313886ce680b3bde00e33bf52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>The units digit of the larger number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the units digit of the smaller number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the positive difference between the numbers is 8. There is only one answer choice that has this units digit, and that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d426991ff8892cefcf8448fb9ba69be57601607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} ~14{,}238}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"104\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>(Similar to MRENTHUSIASM's solution)\n</p><p>~AARUSHGORADIA18\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jPzcN0KeJ88&amp;t=132s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jPzcN0KeJ88&amp;t=132s</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SEp9flDYm2c\">https://youtu.be/SEp9flDYm2c</a>\n</p><p>~ Education, the study Of Everything\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hMqA8i8a2SQ&amp;list=PLexHyfQ8DMuKqltG3cHT7Di4jhVl6L4YJ&amp;index=3\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hMqA8i8a2SQ&amp;list=PLexHyfQ8DMuKqltG3cHT7Di4jhVl6L4YJ&amp;index=3</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P5al76DxyHY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P5al76DxyHY</a> (Hawk Math)\n</p><p>OmegaLearn (Using Algebra and Meta-solving)===\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/d2musztzDjw\">https://youtu.be/d2musztzDjw</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VpYmQEKcBpA\">https://youtu.be/VpYmQEKcBpA</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/50CThrk3RcM?t=107\">https://youtu.be/50CThrk3RcM?t=107</a> (for AMC 10A)\n~TheBeautyofMath\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rEWS75W0Q54?t=198\">https://youtu.be/rEWS75W0Q54?t=198</a> (for AMC 12A)\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/CupJpUzKPB0\">https://youtu